From: AutoBleem <autobleem@retromenele.pl>
Subject: [PATCH] menu_pixel_aspect / menu_safe_margin: the menu on a CRT's non-square pixels

RetroArch 1.22.2 lays the menu out on the window as if its pixels were square and draws to the very edges.
On the console's CRT output (720x480 shown 4:3, a pixel is 8:9) XMB, Ozone and RGUI come out 12.5 % too wide,
and the header, footer and ribbon run into the tube's overscan. Two new settings, identity at their defaults:

  menu_pixel_aspect  (float, 1.0)  width / height of one output pixel; 0.888889 for 720x480 at 4:3
  menu_safe_margin   (uint %, 0)   share of the window kept free on every side (0..25)

The menu, the display widgets and the on-screen text are laid out in a virtual screen: the window less the
margin, its width multiplied by menu_pixel_aspect (720x480, 8/9, 5 %: 576x432, square pixels, exactly 4:3).
video_driver_get_size(), video_info->width/height and the size handed to the menu's render() and to
gfx_animation_update() are the virtual size, so no menu driver or widget needs a change; the GL driver maps
the virtual screen onto the window: gfx_display_gl2_draw(), the scissor begin/end, gl2_set_viewport() for
the font (glyphs get the stretch too) and the RGUI menu texture. A rect spanning the whole virtual width
(height) is stretched to the window's edge on that axis, so wallpaper, ribbon and dimming still fill the
margin. video_driver_get_physical_size() is the window's own size. GL2 only (the console's video driver);
the mouse/touch pointer is not mapped (the console has pads only).
---
diff --git a/config.def.h b/config.def.h
index a2f36da..3d96c7e 100644
--- a/config.def.h
+++ b/config.def.h
@@ -1556,6 +1556,14 @@
 #endif
 /* Specifies whether display widgets should be scaled
  * automatically using the default menu scale factor */
+/* Pixel aspect (width / height of one output pixel) the menu and the
+ * display widgets are laid out for: 1.0 = square pixels. 8/9 = 0.8889 for
+ * 720x480 shown at 4:3 on a CRT. The menu draws in a virtual screen whose
+ * width is the safe area width times this value, stretched back on output */
+#define DEFAULT_MENU_PIXEL_ASPECT 1.0f
+/* Percent of the window kept free on every side by the menu and the
+ * display widgets (CRT overscan); 0 = the whole window */
+#define DEFAULT_MENU_SAFE_MARGIN 0
 #define DEFAULT_MENU_WIDGET_SCALE_AUTO true
 /* Default scale factor for display widgets when widget
  * auto scaling is disabled (fullscreen mode) */
